   "evidence": "Neither Mathlib nor Tau Ceti has this lemma. `rg 'maxTrivSubmodule' mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/Weights` returns only an unrelated hit at Linear.lean:228. In code/TauCeti, `rg 'weightSpace.*0.*maxTrivSubmodule'` matches only the inline `have hR` at MaxTrivSubmodule.lean:52 and :65.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/BaseChange/MaxTrivSubmodule.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma, e.g. `LieModule.weightSpace_zero : weightSpace M (0 : L \u2192 R) = maxTrivSubmodule R L M`, to `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/BaseChange.lean` or a more basic weights file, and mark it `@[simp]`. Then derive both theorems from it plus `map_zero`, and delete the four `have`s.",
   "issue": "`weightSpace M (0 : Module.Dual R L) = maxTrivSubmodule R L M` is stated only as an inline `have`, so it is not available to users. The same fact is proved again at lines 55, 65 and 68 (`hR`/`hA` in both theorems; `hA` is the same fact over `A`, since `Module.Dual.baseChange A 0 = 0`). It mentions only Mathlib types, so it is general infrastructure.",
   "line": 52
  }
 ],
